<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine rain good for maize, soybeans.</title>
<headline>Argentine rain good for maize, soybeans.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rain throughout Argentine grain areas was impeding wheat harvesting Tuesday but should benefit maize and soybeans, which have had to put up with extreme heat in recent days, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The maize plants were getting a bit stressed by the hot weather, so this rain is just what they needed,&quot; a trader said.</p>
<p>The Argentine government's Meteorological Service forecast the wet weather should continue Tuesday and Wednesday. But temperatures could rise as high as 95 degrees Fahrenheit (36 degrees Celsius) in the northern stretches of the grain belt.</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
